From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jason920612 <jasonya2206@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 18:31:26 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Index waypoint connections both ways and evaluate them once
 per tick

The Guava table scanned every row per lookup and copied entry sets on every position change, and every position change (several per tick per player) re-evaluated all of that entity's connections. Now connections are indexed by player and by waypoint, and moved entities are marked dirty and evaluated once at the end of the tick, before packets are flushed.

diff --git a/net/minecraft/server/MinecraftServer.java b/net/minecraft/server/MinecraftServer.java
index c3bf41af0273e902f881cc070fcef6dd64abb063..109c8fe91a2c39f25d7fe2b93e24863c21295376 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/server/MinecraftServer.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/server/MinecraftServer.java
@@ -1832,6 +1832,13 @@ public abstract class MinecraftServer extends ReentrantBlockableEventLoop<TickTa
             tickable.run();
         }
 
+        // Quire start - evaluate waypoint connections once per tick for everything that moved
+        profiler.popPush("waypoints");
+        for (ServerLevel level : this.getAllLevels()) {
+            level.getWaypointManager().quire$flushDirty();
+        }
+        // Quire end
+
         profiler.popPush("send chunks");
 
         for (ServerPlayer player : this.playerList.getPlayers()) {
